So we are a G Suite customer,
but our specific use case here

00:24:17.330 --> 00:24:19.640
is in our warehouse operations.

00:24:19.640 --> 00:24:23.385
I think for us at Stitch Fix,
would be fulfill products.

00:24:23.385 --> 00:24:25.010
So how many of you
here in the audience

00:24:25.010 --> 00:24:27.350
are customers of Stitch Fix,
that heard of Stitch Fix?

00:24:27.350 --> 00:24:28.670
Raise of hands.

00:24:28.670 --> 00:24:30.012
The rest of you, sign up.

00:24:30.012 --> 00:24:31.310
[LAUGHTER]

00:24:31.310 --> 00:24:34.960
So just to give you a little bit
of a snippet of how the Stitch

00:24:34.960 --> 00:24:38.510
Fix business model works is that
as you complete your profile

00:24:38.510 --> 00:24:41.360
we have product that's
already in our warehouses

00:24:41.360 --> 00:24:44.780
that we algorithmically
pick and then present it

00:24:44.780 --> 00:24:45.920
to a remote stylist.

00:24:45.920 --> 00:24:50.240
The stylist takes that system
recommendation-- the algorithm

00:24:50.240 --> 00:24:52.990
recommendations-- and then
picks the best products

00:24:52.990 --> 00:24:53.960
suitable for you.

00:24:53.960 --> 00:24:56.810
And then at that point
is where the handoff

00:24:56.810 --> 00:24:59.600
happens to our warehouse
associates in our warehouses.

00:24:59.600 --> 00:25:03.140
We have five
warehouses currently

00:25:03.140 --> 00:25:05.630
in Stitch Fix that we
fulfill product in the US.

00:25:05.630 --> 00:25:08.630
We are expanding into
UK this calendar year.

00:25:13.130 --> 00:25:15.500
We started with the women's
business, launched the men's

00:25:15.500 --> 00:25:16.583
and now we are doing kids.

00:25:16.583 --> 00:25:20.010
So you have no excuse
not to sign up.

00:25:20.010 --> 00:25:25.610
So the touch point from
a warehouse associate's

00:25:25.610 --> 00:25:30.530
standpoint, it is not so much
about the Chrome, the G Suite

00:25:30.530 --> 00:25:32.620
applications, it's
more the applications

00:25:32.620 --> 00:25:36.110
that we built in-house for
our product fulfillment.

00:25:36.110 --> 00:25:38.740
So think of it as
like a product--

00:25:38.740 --> 00:25:41.372
like when you pick a
product in the warehouse.

00:25:41.372 --> 00:25:43.080
So that is the use
case that we're using.

00:25:43.080 --> 00:25:45.710
So we have, as I said, we have
five different warehouses.

00:25:45.710 --> 00:25:51.320
We have workers that sign
into the applications

00:25:51.320 --> 00:25:54.110
that they need to interact
with through a barcode scanner.

00:25:54.110 --> 00:25:55.970
So what you can
see in this image

00:25:55.970 --> 00:25:59.600
is the Chrome device attached
to our simple barcode scanner

00:25:59.600 --> 00:26:00.830
and attached to a cart.

00:26:00.830 --> 00:26:03.140
So the cart is where
we pick the product.

00:26:03.140 --> 00:26:07.130
So we authenticate
through their badge

00:26:07.130 --> 00:26:09.950
to put them into the profile
that they need to be.

00:26:09.950 --> 00:26:12.200
And then from there, they
have the set of applications

00:26:12.200 --> 00:26:13.617
that they're
authorized to access.

00:26:13.617 --> 00:26:16.580
So all of our applications that
we use for the Chrome device

00:26:16.580 --> 00:26:19.940
are browser native--

00:26:19.940 --> 00:26:21.125
browser-based applications.

00:26:21.125 --> 00:26:22.250
There's no client involved.

00:26:22.250 --> 00:26:24.500
As far as Chrome
made a lot of sense

00:26:24.500 --> 00:26:27.030
to put that on the front line.

00:26:27.030 --> 00:26:30.870
So for us it is most not
only the cost effectiveness.

00:26:30.870 --> 00:26:34.460
I think the ability to have
those applications easily

00:26:34.460 --> 00:26:34.970
accessible.

00:26:34.970 --> 00:26:37.160
So once you're authenticated,
you know the apps

00:26:37.160 --> 00:26:39.470
that you need to use, and
they would essentially

00:26:39.470 --> 00:26:43.160
push this cart around the
warehouse to pick product.

00:26:43.160 --> 00:26:46.520
So it made it more
compelling for us

00:26:46.520 --> 00:26:48.380
to use because I
think the battery

00:26:48.380 --> 00:26:52.040
life, the cost of the devices,
all of those factored in as we

00:26:52.040 --> 00:26:53.480
looked at these devices.

00:26:53.480 --> 00:26:56.398
And it made the process
that much more easier.

00:26:56.398 --> 00:26:58.190
So just to give you a
little bit of history

00:26:58.190 --> 00:27:01.430
about when these Chrome
devices came into play,

00:27:01.430 --> 00:27:03.850
it was not something that
was provisioned by IT.

00:27:03.850 --> 00:27:05.390
IT had no involvement in it.

00:27:05.390 --> 00:27:07.190
The operations and the
warehouse operations

00:27:07.190 --> 00:27:08.910
were procuring these devices.

00:27:08.910 --> 00:27:13.190
So we have over 2,400
devices in our portfolio.

00:27:13.190 --> 00:27:15.020
And those are now--

00:27:15.020 --> 00:27:20.270
in the past year, as we brought
on Chrome Enterprise device

00:27:20.270 --> 00:27:23.450
management, IT has
now taken over it.

00:27:23.450 --> 00:27:25.600
So we are managing
the end point,

00:27:25.600 --> 00:27:28.970
we are managing the
plugins, and so on.

00:27:28.970 --> 00:27:32.240
So it made a lot of sense
for us to use Chrome devices.

00:27:32.240 --> 00:27:35.460
And we not only use
it in the warehouse,

00:27:35.460 --> 00:27:38.142
but we also, when
workers change shifts

00:27:38.142 --> 00:27:40.350
it just makes that interaction
that much more easier.

00:27:40.350 --> 00:27:43.260
So the employee experience
there is consistent.

00:27:43.260 --> 00:27:47.777
And they move from one
location to another location.

00:27:47.777 --> 00:27:49.610
They don't take the
Chrome device with them.

00:27:49.610 --> 00:27:51.610
They leave the cart there,
go to the next place,

00:27:51.610 --> 00:27:55.520
sign out here, sign back in,
and then they continue to work.

00:27:55.520 --> 00:27:59.240
And the add on value for
us was as we looked at--

00:27:59.240 --> 00:28:01.910
because we are a G Suite
customer-- we have data

00:28:01.910 --> 00:28:04.610
that we capture through
G Suite application,

00:28:04.610 --> 00:28:07.430
so that either in Google
Sheets or a Google

00:28:07.430 --> 00:28:10.280
Docs where the workers
that are in the facility

00:28:10.280 --> 00:28:13.420
picking product, if
they are some QA issue

00:28:13.420 --> 00:28:16.550
or whatever, they would go on
to toggle over to the Google

00:28:16.550 --> 00:28:19.190
Sheets and then make notes in
there so that their supervisors

00:28:19.190 --> 00:28:20.417
can interact with them.

00:28:20.417 --> 00:28:22.500
So they are not only using
it for picking product,

00:28:22.500 --> 00:28:27.200
it also works as a
collaborative device.

00:28:27.200 --> 00:28:31.360
So we've standardized on the
Chrome browser at Stitch Fix.

00:28:31.360 --> 00:28:33.310
So it's pretty
much everybody that

00:28:33.310 --> 00:28:35.700
interacts with our
applications, both internal

00:28:35.700 --> 00:28:37.270
or our public
cloud applications,

00:28:37.270 --> 00:28:40.630
we are using Chrome as
the standard device.

00:28:40.630 --> 00:28:44.320
As I shared earlier, the
Stitch Fix employee population

00:28:44.320 --> 00:28:46.630
consists of like the
information or knowledge

00:28:46.630 --> 00:28:49.630
workers, our customer
service warehouse associates,

00:28:49.630 --> 00:28:51.880
and then we have our
remote stylists that

00:28:51.880 --> 00:28:54.070
are working on their own
devices but they're working

00:28:54.070 --> 00:28:58.180
remote, that work from home.

00:28:58.180 --> 00:29:00.490
For us, standardizing
on a single browser

00:29:00.490 --> 00:29:02.290
made a lot of
sense, and so we've

00:29:02.290 --> 00:29:05.110
optimized our applications
to work well with Chrome.

00:29:05.110 --> 00:29:08.170
We are current use
cases for us as I

00:29:08.170 --> 00:29:10.270
shared earlier is
using Chromebooks

00:29:10.270 --> 00:29:12.400
for warehouse workers.

00:29:12.400 --> 00:29:16.720
And we're also evaluating
Pixel Books as an option

00:29:16.720 --> 00:29:17.860
for our knowledge workers.

00:29:17.860 --> 00:29:21.190
So interestingly, one of
our c-level executives

00:29:21.190 --> 00:29:25.530
who came on board recently,
she challenged us,

00:29:25.530 --> 00:29:28.200
say like, hey, how come you
get the provisioning Windows

00:29:28.200 --> 00:29:30.190
and Mac devices, why
not Chrome devices?

00:29:30.190 --> 00:29:31.870
Because she had
her own Chromebook,

00:29:31.870 --> 00:29:34.990
she was used to it in the past,
and it just made sense for us

00:29:34.990 --> 00:29:35.990
to kind of explore that.

00:29:35.990 --> 00:29:39.780
So we are now exploring
Pixel Book as an option for--

00:29:39.780 --> 00:29:42.400
as an alternate because
everything is in the cloud,

00:29:42.400 --> 00:29:44.350
and they don't have a
lot of compute needs,

00:29:44.350 --> 00:29:46.463
and it made it that
much more compelling

00:29:46.463 --> 00:29:47.630
for us to put that in there.

00:29:47.630 --> 00:29:50.530
So now that is slowly
part of our portfolio.

00:29:50.530 --> 00:29:52.605
And we're also
currently evaluating

00:29:52.605 --> 00:29:54.730
about standardizing on
Chromebooks for the stylists

00:29:54.730 --> 00:29:56.920
who are currently on a BYOD.

00:29:56.920 --> 00:30:01.120
Because we don't have visibility
to that end point held,

00:30:01.120 --> 00:30:03.400
and that's, from a
security perspective,

00:30:03.400 --> 00:30:04.520
is a bit challenging.

00:30:04.520 --> 00:30:08.440
So we are exploring about
potentially making a Chrome

00:30:08.440 --> 00:30:13.690
device available if the device
that the remote stylist has

00:30:13.690 --> 00:30:17.780
today is not compliant, or it's
not up to speed, up to date.

00:30:17.780 --> 00:30:19.720
So there's another extension.

00:30:19.720 --> 00:30:23.230
So we started with
just the browser,

00:30:23.230 --> 00:30:25.830
the warehouse workers now
looking at other use cases

00:30:25.830 --> 00:30:26.330
as well.

00:30:29.480 --> 00:30:31.480
I think one of the
things that I know

00:30:31.480 --> 00:30:33.630
as customer service,
customer experience that

00:30:33.630 --> 00:30:35.110
are important for
the organization,

00:30:35.110 --> 00:30:37.420
far as employee experience
also is critical,

00:30:37.420 --> 00:30:41.170
because these workers who
are interacting on the Chrome

00:30:41.170 --> 00:30:43.570
browser, especially
at the warehouse,

00:30:43.570 --> 00:30:45.670
we've set up kiosk
devices where people

00:30:45.670 --> 00:30:49.030
can log in and deal with their
email or any of their employee

00:30:49.030 --> 00:30:49.760
communication.

00:30:49.760 --> 00:30:54.250
So it has helped us kind of
make that consistent message

00:30:54.250 --> 00:30:57.190
across when they are on the
shop floor, versus when they're

00:30:57.190 --> 00:30:59.110
in the office space,
when they need to attend

00:30:59.110 --> 00:31:01.540
to HR or personal issues.

00:31:01.540 --> 00:31:06.010
And for us it has been, I
think that the collaboration

00:31:06.010 --> 00:31:07.630
capabilities is tremendous.

00:31:07.630 --> 00:31:10.150
It just really helps
us keep up-to-date.

00:31:10.150 --> 00:31:13.990
And so far we have no
reported security incidents.

00:31:13.990 --> 00:31:15.670
So that's actually
comforting for us.

00:31:15.670 --> 00:31:18.720
I can sleep well.

00:31:18.720 --> 00:31:20.100
All right.

00:31:20.100 --> 00:31:21.948
Mike, back to you.

00:31:21.948 --> 00:31:23.490
I think we still
have plenty of time.

00:31:23.490 --> 00:31:23.920
MIKE DAOUST: All right.

00:31:23.920 --> 00:31:24.600
Great.

00:31:24.600 --> 00:31:25.120
Thank you.

00:31:25.120 --> 00:31:26.400
Thank you very much, Ravi.

00:31:26.400 --> 00:31:27.180
That was super.

00:31:27.180 --> 00:31:29.618
And I think it's always
great to have a customer

00:31:29.618 --> 00:31:30.660
sort of bring it to life.

00:31:30.660 --> 00:31:34.013
And as you can tell from Ravi's
experience-- and a lot of it's

00:31:34.013 --> 00:31:35.430
a testament to his
leadership-- is

00:31:35.430 --> 00:31:38.610
that the use cases
have grown up not just

00:31:38.610 --> 00:31:41.790
within the frontline segment,
but also the C-suite,

00:31:41.790 --> 00:31:45.330
and really asking the questions
around why not move to Chrome?

00:31:45.330 --> 00:31:47.400
Why not move things
more to the cloud?

00:31:47.400 --> 00:31:49.800
Just given both the customer
experience as well as

00:31:49.800 --> 00:31:52.500
the IT savings that's
associated with that.

00:31:52.500 --> 00:31:55.550
[MUSIC PLAYING]

